iterations.reply:
Operations' two additions are left out. The node's declared capabilities are only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`. It has no filesystem or `http-client` import, and the target is `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with no WASI. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` or calling the metadata service would need new capability imports in the graph. Sending the input's text to an external service would also leak data beyond the node's granted authority. If either is wanted, it should be added to the graph as an explicit capability. The node below just sends the reply and returns the host's confirmation.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        crate::aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

